  "aciklama": "Colgan 3407 stalled and crashed into a house near Buffalo. The cause: inappropriate response to the stick shaker, deepening an aerodynamic stall.\n\nFailure chain: Speed decays on approach → Stick shaker activates → Captain pulls back → Stall deepens → Aircraft crashes\n\nRelated episode: The Hidden Flaw Inside United 232 — https://youtu.be/BukKRJfO7zI\n\nSeries — Aviation Failures: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLHIwDgtDRNyY\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Colgan Air Flight 3407（N200WQ） wreckage.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Colgan_Air_Flight_3407%EF%BC%88N200WQ%EF%BC%89_wreckage.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Wreckage of N200WQ.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wreckage_of_N200WQ.jpg\n• Archival film: \"ILS RWY 23 KBUF.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ILS_RWY_23_KBUF.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Obama and Beverly Eckert.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obama_and_Beverly_Eckert.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Colgan Air Flight 3407 — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colgan_Air_Flight_3407\n• NTSB — AAR1001 (cited by Wikipedia) — https://www.ntsb.gov/investigations/AccidentReports/Reports/AAR1001.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 28 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #Colgan3407 #aviation #history",
